From cfe0aeff792aacdfbbb53df8fb596717287daf05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(scheduler): add a first-fit scheduler over a static
 inventory

Nothing implemented the Scheduler contract, so the reconciler could
never allocate accelerators. FirstFitScheduler allocates from a static
inventory of nodes and accelerator devices, read from the JSON file
named by FORGEMESH_INVENTORY_FILE and validated strictly: unknown
fields, implicit type coercion, empty lists and duplicate ids are
errors, so that the control plane can refuse to start on a broken
file.

allocate() takes the first node, in inventory order, that has enough
free devices of the requested type with at least minMemoryGiB each,
and records the allocation together with its devices through
SQLiteRegistry.create_allocation, so device exclusivity stays enforced
by the database. Allocations are serialized within one scheduler:
under first-fit, concurrent requests all pick the same free device and
the losers would run out of retries while devices were still free. A
conflict caused by another connection is retried a bounded number of
times.

The same idempotency key returns the same allocation, also after a
restart. A resource that already holds an allocation that still fits
(a new generation that kept the accelerator request) keeps it; one
that no longer fits is a conflict until it is released. feasible()
only reads, and release() is idempotent. No lease is set: the
reconciler releases the allocation when the resource is deleted.
